  data: {
    LLM: "If your team wins the bid, protect your Pedros! If you have a Pedro (5), try to play it when your partner is winning the trick with a high card (like the Ace or King). If the opponent wins a trick containing a Pedro, they get the 5 points, and you likely fail your bid.\n\nThe 'King Trap': Since the King is worth 30 points (nearly half the round), do not play it early. Wait until you have drained the opponents of their lower trumps or until you are certain your partner can shield you with an Ace. Conversely, if you have the Ace, lead it instantly to smoke out the opponent's King.\n\nBidding Density: Because there are 63 points available, a bid of 40 is considered standard for a strong hand. If you bid 60+, you are effectively calling a 'Slam'. Only bid this high if you hold the King, Ace, and both Pedros. Defensively, if you see the opponents are close to their bid, sacrifice your Nine to prevent them from taking the King.",
    Player: "If your team wins the bid, protect your Pedros! If you have a Pedro (5), try to play it when your partner is winning the trick with a high card (like the Ace or King). If the opponent wins a trick containing a Pedro, they get the 5 points, and you likely fail your bid.\n\nThe 'King Trap': Since the King is worth 30 points (nearly half the round), do not play it early. Wait until you have drained the opponents of their lower trumps or until you are certain your partner can shield you with an Ace. Conversely, if you have the Ace, lead it instantly to smoke out the opponent's King.\n\nBidding Density: Because there are 63 points available, a bid of 40 is considered standard for a strong hand. If you bid 60+, you are effectively calling a 'Slam'. Only bid this high if you hold the King, Ace, and both Pedros. Defensively, if you see the opponents are close to their bid, sacrifice your Nine to prevent them from taking the King.",
